%% # Scene 11 — spur, analyzer error during sampling with the needle down, operator recovery
%% # Same situation as scene 05, on a spur. On error the analyzer sends Status (Error) and
%% # Sample Complete; the carrier is released only after Status (Ready).
%% # Carrier flow: right to left on the Main-Lane; the spur rises perpendicular to it.
%% # Coordinates are in a fixed 1920x1080 space (track panel: x 30..950, y 120..885).
%% # Points left of x=30 or right of x=950 are outside the panel (hidden).
%% geometry spur
%% subtitle Spur — analyzer error with the needle down, operator recovery
sequenceDiagram
    participant IF as Interface
    participant AN as Analyzer
    participant DMX as DMX

    %% carrier id=C1 sid=SID-000123

    %% caption 1 · Spur | A carrier holding a sample tube travels along the Main-Lane towards the spur of the analyzer interface.
    %% at 2.2
    %% move C1 to antenna2
    %% on antenna1 C1
    %% caption 2 · Diverted — Prepare — Sample Acquisition | The carrier is diverted without stopping into a short piece of pit-lane that turns into the spur: Prepare. The gate stops it on the sampling point of the up branch: Sample Acquisition.
    %% on antenna1
    IF->>AN: Prepare SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    %% id ok-c1
    AN-->>IF: OK SampleId=SID-000123
    %% on antenna2
    %% id sample-acquisition-c1
    IF->>AN: Sample Acquisition SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 ok-c1
    %% id query-c1
    AN->>DMX: Query SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 sample-acquisition-c1
    %% for C1
    %% id ok-c1-2
    AN-->>IF: OK
    %% after 0.1 query-c1
    DMX-->>AN: Tests to perform SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 ok-c1-2
    %% caption 3 · Test query — Aspiration | After the reply to Prepare the analyzer has asked DMX (LIS) which tests to perform. Now its needle goes down into the tube and it starts aspirating.
    %% after 0.1 ok-c1-2
    %% needle sp down
    %% after 0.1 ok-c1-2
    %% duration 2.6
    Note over AN: Pipetting Analyzer - SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% caption 4 · Instrument error | During aspiration the analyzer goes into error, leaving the needle down in the tube. It immediately sends its status (Error) and Sample Complete. The interface replies OK to the status.
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% status analyzer error
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% id status
    AN->>IF: Status State=Error
    %% id sample-complete-c1
    AN->>IF: Sample Complete SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.3 status
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 0.1 sample-complete-c1
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 2.1 status
    %% caption 5 · Operator recovery | Sample Complete is not enough: with the analyzer in error the carrier stays still, the needle is in the tube. An operator comes to the instrument for a recovery: the needle goes back up.
    %% after 2.1 status
    %% operator analyzer duration=7
    %% after 2.1 status
    %% duration 6
    Note over AN: Operator recovery
    %% after 4.6 status
    %% needle sp up duration=1.2
    %% after 2.6
    %% caption 6 · Instrument ready | The instrument is green again: it sends its status (Ready) to the interface, which replies OK. Only now the carrier is released.
    %% after 2.6 needle sp
    %% status analyzer ready
    %% after 2.6 needle sp
    %% id status-2
    AN->>IF: Status State=Ready
    %% after 0.2
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 1.5 status-2
    %% status analyzer normal
    %% after 1.9 status-2
    %% pass antenna2 C1
    %% on antenna3 C1
    %% caption 7 · Release | The carrier went round the spur and has left the interface module: the interface sends Release.
    %% on antenna3
    IF->>AN: Release SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
